# Drop folder for TradingView Pine chart-data exports used by ../tools/compare_eq.py.
# Ad-hoc exports are large, local-only scratch — never commit them.
*.csv

# 🔴 EXCEPT golden/ — ONE committed export per engine, so the parity gate can run on EVERY
# clone, on every machine, in CI, forever. Before this existed, whether a gate could run at
# all depended on which CSVs happened to be sitting on one laptop: on 2026-09-09 NINE of the
# fourteen gates could not answer, so rule 22 ("no engine change without a green gate") was
# unsatisfiable and therefore blocked work instead of gating it.
#
# ⚠ The golden export does a DIFFERENT job from a fresh one, and you need both:
#     golden  → REGRESSION. Catches the PYTHON drifting. Always available, runs in seconds.
#     fresh   → ACCEPTANCE. Catches the PINE and the Python disagreeing after a Pine change.
#   A golden export can only ever prove the engine still does what it did when the file was
#   taken. It says NOTHING about a Pine edit made afterwards. Do not let a green golden run
#   stand in for a fresh export when the indicator has moved.
!golden/
!golden/*.csv
